{"title":"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A trapezoid has side lengths 3, 5, 7, and 11. The sum of all the possible areas of the trapezoid can be written in the form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb9397757c1d24bd08941c46ba15f3746284b1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1\\sqrt{n_1}+r_2\\sqrt{n_2}+r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae5f496b8ddda88b5cbbc06ccb02bee0580fd0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> are rational numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/defbf06b987965438e5928b96688e48df84cba0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c5df946080fc6ec1ee0a560a8e8c5e6699113c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers not divisible by the square of any prime. What is the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/627a25c9f3b44f4ec9b74bd974fc435518bde6fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1+r_2+r_3+n_1+n_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"171\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6651a35e8a435f4927e3f15518ee6a3fbaf3d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 57\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 59\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 61\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 63\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Name the trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d4164af5279f09df6795ff87d95768e3f8d993b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB&lt;CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/f/bbf6ac338f42fb945181c3550fdd05662ce0d8ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD&lt;BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />. Draw a line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, crossing the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be4bef340c104973fc51495184b03babcf31562e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=AD$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36e89f3158194a1a4ebfc0154a9067013a8afcc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC=DC-DE=DC-AB$\" width=\"239\" height=\"13\" />. One needs to guarantee that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/2/5425119121bf8243c6736bceaa2a7b044857bcf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE+EC&gt;BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"14\" />, so there are only three possible trapezoids:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b1a3c7e16e90233a8e27b4c50449a51cacba59.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB=3, BC=7, CD=11, DA=5, CE=8\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/303076341b6d55608d37aca2e32de546ce55bac9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB=5, BC=7, CD=11, DA=3, CE=6\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bdd388fd1dc76c6bff58b22648b5f9d5b3f8e166.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB=7, BC=5, CD=11, DA=3, CE=4\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIn the first case, by Law of Cosines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10d31e7a7201d3dc0649af9f52f729fcf0e08b1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle BCD) = (8^2+7^2-5^2)/(2\\cdot 7\\cdot 8) = 11/14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"377\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb9e6648923f50989f12b78fc1baae7c9610636.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (\\angle BCD) = \\sqrt{1-121/196} = 5\\sqrt{3}/14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"315\" height=\"32\" />. Therefore the area of this trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f469253e29f63adce61dd3e24e587bef962d669f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} (3+11) \\cdot 7 \\cdot 5\\sqrt{3}/14 = \\frac{35}{2}\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"243\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>In the second case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90ce98307b81c7376a75c8685c5e024b33a067b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle BCD) = (6^2+7^2-3^2)/(2\\cdot 6\\cdot 7) = 19/21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"373\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8effb745af7b2a85aff2d3a96656c3f46bdb948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (\\angle BCD) = \\sqrt{1-361/441} = 4\\sqrt{5}/21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"314\" height=\"32\" />. Therefore the area of this trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87ce080b9e03db09dcbc163451fbf76bad59e7e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} (5+11) \\cdot 7 \\cdot 4\\sqrt{5}/21 =\\frac{32}{3}\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"243\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>In the third case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4895429fb262e1d3caa5546693da0a08c0e5f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCD = 90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" />, therefore the area of this trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bd09030829c6705978562569b3956eebe21f1cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} (7+11) \\cdot 3 = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"141\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/a/f4a1d47aebe116df6a3b1467b3150b57e1a340a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 + r_2 + r_3 + n_1 + n_2 = 17.5 + 10.666... + 27 + 3 + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"419\" height=\"15\" />, which rounds down to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddfe60e8bbc8a75dab33c2f3a2b04598b75bdc5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 63}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2012AMC12BProblem20Solution2.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/7e/2012AMC12BProblem20Solution2.PNG/500px-2012AMC12BProblem20Solution2.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"380\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/7e/2012AMC12BProblem20Solution2.PNG/750px-2012AMC12BProblem20Solution2.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/7e/2012AMC12BProblem20Solution2.PNG/1000px-2012AMC12BProblem20Solution2.PNG 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let the area of the trapezoid be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, the area of the triangle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, the area of the parallelogram be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4caea56d945d0b6e49701b42ce06e0fb92e663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>By <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heron%27s_formula\">Heron's Formula</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/8/3c8d464c39d94de874264b37c050dbc13ebb3d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1 = \\sqrt{\\frac{b+c+d-a}{2} \\cdot \\frac{c+d-a-b}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a+b+d-c}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b+c-a-d}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"523\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f25ef6a3f7c707785776b4464405911e187db14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2 = \\frac{S_1 \\cdot 2}{c-a} \\cdot a = \\frac{2aS_1}{c-a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"180\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b57085b56f48674e192238b38b1fd8f6e0d18e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = S_1 + S_2 = S_1(1+\\frac{2a}{c-a}) = S_1 \\cdot \\frac{c+a}{c-a} = \\frac14 \\cdot \\frac{c+a}{c-a} \\cdot \\sqrt{(b+c+d-a)(c+d-a-b)(a+b+d-c)(b+c-a-d)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"917\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b3c27171aba2140505212ce5b912115d1cdd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c122a5f4ffcb58a92ffc845df880b199f6571c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a14feb8723914a3ef109c8ff5ce8871141f66f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e06ffe5b2cf71c23bc7079c1cd268da267d2049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 5$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/e/cbed7259817b0509c073067d90ca4e187d015151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\frac14 \\cdot \\frac{14}{8} \\cdot \\sqrt{(7+11+5-3)(11+5-3-7)(3+7+5-11)(7+11-3-5)} = \\frac{35\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"693\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b3c27171aba2140505212ce5b912115d1cdd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d78ed94215e8e444e06174a1f8666665be7b720d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb45ac08f0a40da167c4e3ade6cb5639057bcc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 5$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d2ebc78ee3a2e67ae89407f1312323d25bc80ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 7$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a72baa0cdde90177fec47fc0b462ffde51f9fae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\frac14 \\cdot \\frac{8}{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{(11+5+7-3)(5+7-3-11)(3+5+7-11)(11+5-3-7)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"613\" height=\"38\" />, which is impossible as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/63446c1ad03d320ba34290509c0d3cd41569aea1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+7-3-11 = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b3c27171aba2140505212ce5b912115d1cdd69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add0bf97955f4eedafea7db58ac66eb4a130baa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/4180920f7b814184d4bd9e5d514cb86910cfb250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca1e09711b2d3dfc92eabbf9561644fc87527f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/9/c693ccc6502d0c75a071bb17b85c3c7ea3928124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\frac14 \\cdot \\frac{10}{4} \\cdot \\sqrt{(5+7+11-3)(7+11-3-5)(3+5+11-7)(5+7-11-3)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"623\" height=\"38\" />, which is impossible as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/0/4c04f3b394a03ebaa7b461b602e27541efed558e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+7-11-3 = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72e2e58a2ef8bb4eedd627c212f63bb8f507301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 5$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d78ed94215e8e444e06174a1f8666665be7b720d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/4180920f7b814184d4bd9e5d514cb86910cfb250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e7679b01e114773e2822a8fd5615ea83def33c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 3$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20bb5cf1cca81d40b70c84f3267d1f07b8bdd0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\frac14 \\cdot \\frac{12}{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{(11+7+3-5)(7+3-5-11)(5+11+3-7)(11+7-5-3)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"623\" height=\"38\" />, which is impossible as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/d/9ddceb9fe3b304517abd2584829b404858a67e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+3-5-11 = -6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72e2e58a2ef8bb4eedd627c212f63bb8f507301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 5$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246ec286b9641f91f9dfa14932e47171e2fad854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a14feb8723914a3ef109c8ff5ce8871141f66f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d2ebc78ee3a2e67ae89407f1312323d25bc80ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 7$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca2ce783213021aee8e97cdd0a46264d5630d18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\frac14 \\cdot \\frac{16}{6} \\cdot \\sqrt{(3+11+7-5)(11+7-5-3)(5+3+7-11)(3+11-5-7)} = \\frac{32\\sqrt{5}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"693\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b1838491bea2799f90f459e5a942e9dd6d7c4c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246ec286b9641f91f9dfa14932e47171e2fad854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a14feb8723914a3ef109c8ff5ce8871141f66f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e06ffe5b2cf71c23bc7079c1cd268da267d2049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 5$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/325ad56f565d3e285d2250c9ffe6f9af31512858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\frac14 \\cdot \\frac{18}{4} \\cdot \\sqrt{(3+11+5-7)(11+5-7-)(7+5+5-11)(3+11-7-5)} = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"648\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de2af47944e56a4dea74cdc1f18c59f0f07c31ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{35}{2} + \\frac{32}{3} + 27 + 3 + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"171\" height=\"38\" />, which rounds down to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/562e6965fded90fac865ce52cf24236a598306c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 63}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p><p>Note: the three invalid cases can also be determined by the triangle inequality.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/8w1vrsD2urs\">https://youtu.be/8w1vrsD2urs</a>  ~Math Problem Solving Skills\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B\">2012 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3